  "raw": {
    "https://peace.peopleadmin.com/postings/3080": {
      "title": "William Peace University Portal | Adjunct Instructor, Philosophy (Continuous Recruitment)",
      "description": "William Peace University Portal | Adjunct Instructor, Philosophy (Continuous Recruitment) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Careers Log In /Create Account Help Benefits of Working at WPU Adjunct Instructor, Philosophy (Continuous Recruitment) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Positing Details Position Information Position Title: Adjunct Instructor, Philosophy (Continuous Recruitment) Posting Number: WPU0063417 University Information: William Peace University (“Peace”) provides a culture that fosters an energized team environment, builds on our strengths, promotes creativity and innovation, and encourages respect and open communication. We value our faculty and staff. We know they are important and vital to the growth of our university and culture. Senior leadership is personally dedicated to the professional growth and development of each employee. We want to help you build your career, while ensuring you have great work-life balance and flexibility. We teach our students the skills needed for ethical citizenship, not just in the classroom, but by example. We believe in giving back to our community, and our employees take pride in working at Peace. Department: Humanities Purpose of Department: The Department of Humanities is a multi-disciplinary department which provides an immersive, hands-on learning experience for Traditional Undergraduate and Peace Online students. Summary of Position: William Peace University is continuously seeking qualified scholars for adjunct faculty positions in the Philosophy discipline who have demonstrated commitment to the promotion of interdisciplinary work and teaching excellence and who possess a collaborative leadership style. The successful candidate should have knowledge of and experience in their selected teaching discipline, as well as experience with and the ability to use instructional technologies to support classroom activities. Applications are accepted on a rolling basis and are reviewed as vacancies arise within the department. Essential duties and responsibilities: Teaching assignments would include lecture instruction in courses for the Department of Humanities in the Philosophy discipline. Assignments may include classroom courses, online distance-education courses, or both. Depending on the department’s needs, selected candidates will be offered contracts to teach one or more course-sections for semester. Minimum Qualifications: • A Master’s degree in the teaching discipline, or a Master’s degree with a concentration in the teaching discipline (minimum of 18 graduate semester hours in discipline) • A demonstrated commitment to undergraduate teaching • Related work experiences in the field, professional licensure and certifications, honors and awards, continuous documented excellence in teaching, or other demonstrated competencies and achievements that contribute to effective teaching and student learning outcomes may be used to supplement academic credentials if warranted • Established record of teaching excellence and demonstrated leadership experience. • A minimum of two years of work experience required Preferred Qualifications: • Ph.D. in the teaching discipline • 1-2 years teaching experience at the undergraduate level Hours per week: Varies by course load Job Posting Date: 07/14/2026 Priority Deadline: 12/31/2028 Priority Deadline Information: Priority consideration will be given to applications received by the Priority Date; however, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Teaching Evaluations William Peace University 15 East Peace Street Raleigh, NC 27604 919.508.2000 Back to top Copyright © William Peace University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://peace.peopleadmin.com/postings/3098": {
      "title": "William Peace University Portal | Administrative Assistant and Internal Events Coordinator",
      "description": "William Peace University Portal | Administrative Assistant and Internal Events Coordinator Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Careers Log In /Create Account Help Benefits of Working at WPU Administrative Assistant and Internal Events Coordinator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Positing Details Position Information Position Title: Administrative Assistant and Internal Events Coordinator Posting Number: WPU0063917 University Information: William Peace University (“Peace”) provides a culture that fosters an energized team environment, builds on our strengths, promotes creativity and innovation, and encourages respect and open communication. We value our faculty and staff. We know they are important and vital to the growth of our university and culture. Senior leadership is personally dedicated to the professional growth and development of each employee. We want to help you build your career, while ensuring you have great work-life balance and flexibility. We teach our students the skills needed for ethical citizenship, not just in the classroom, but by example. We believe in giving back to our community, and our employees take pride in working at Peace. Department: Finance and Administration Purpose of Department: The Department of Finance and Administration is responsible for providing exceptional service and oversight of accounting; purchasing; contracting; budget development; cost controls; financial modeling and forecasting; investment management; facilities; public safety; information technology; human resources; as well as bookstore and food services outsourcing. Summary of Position: The Administrative Assistant and Internal Events Coordinator is an essential member of the Finance and Administration team, and is responsible for providing administrative support to the Vice President of Administration/ CFO . The Administrative Assistant performs duties supporting the Vice President and the division as a whole and supports administrative efforts related to Board of Trustees functions and meetings. Additionally, this position performs secondary duties related to managing the University’s internal events calendar and spaces. This position produces correspondence, enters invoices, manages files, handles mail, manages calendars, and orders supplies and materials. Essential duties and responsibilities: Primary: Administrative Support Supports the Vice President for Administration/ CFO in all office/administrative activities Prepares financial transactions (invoices, purchase orders, check requests), makes purchases, and reconciles credit card statements for expenses incurred by the CFO . Maintains overall office environment for all offices under the CFO’s purview, including ordering supplies and ensuring stock of office materials. Drafts emails and correspondence on behalf of the CFO Serves as “back up” to the Executive Assistant to the President for taking minutes at Board of Trustees and other meetings. Manages the CFO’s calendar by scheduling appointments and meetings. Organizes and manages files. Supports the CFO in creating materials for Board and other presentations. Builds and maintains positive working relationships with team members, internal customers, and external vendors Coordinates travel for the CFO as needed Secondary: Internal Events Manages the “Active Calendar” system which includes room bookings (non-classroom) and the public-facing calendar on the University’s website Serve as a liaison between departments hosting internal events and dining services, facilities, public safety, and IT in coordinating event setup and logistics Assist the Academic Affairs Operations Specialist in planning the University’s annual Commencement ceremony Collaborate with other campus partners who manage internal and external calendars including the Director of External Relations and Events (external events) and the Academic Affairs Operations Specialist (classroom and academic calendar) Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in related field plus two years of relevant experience or equivalent combination of education and experience. Must have strong computer skills including Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, PowerPoint); excellent written and verbal communication skills; strong organization skills with extreme attention to detail; ability to exercise extreme confidentiality and integrity; and a service-oriented attitude. Equivalent combinations of experience and education may be considered. Preferred Qualifications: Experience in higher education or non-profit environment Events planning experience Hours per week: 40 Job Posting Date: 07/29/2026 Priority Deadline: 08/12/2026 Priority Deadline Information: Priority consideration will be given to applications received by the Priority Date; however, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation William Peace University 15 East Peace Street Raleigh, NC 27604 919.508.2000 Back to top Copyright © William Peace University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://peace.peopleadmin.com/postings/2796": {
      "title": "William Peace University Portal | Adjunct Instructor, Department of Culture, History &amp; Politics (Continuous Recruitment)",
      "description": "William Peace University Portal | Adjunct Instructor, Department of Culture, History &amp; Politics (Continuous Recruitment) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Careers Log In /Create Account Help Benefits of Working at WPU Adjunct Instructor, Department of Culture, History & Politics (Continuous Recruitment) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Positing Details Position Information Position Title: Adjunct Instructor, Department of Culture, History & Politics (Continuous Recruitment) Posting Number: WPU0003017 University Information: WPU provides a culture that fosters an energized team environment, builds on our strengths, promotes creativity and innovation, and encourages respect and open communication. We value our faculty and staff. We know they are important and vital to the growth of our university and culture. Senior leadership is personally dedicated to the professional growth and development of each employee. We want to help you build your career, while ensuring you have great work-life balance and flexibility. We teach our students the skills needed for ethical citizenship, not just in the classroom, but by example. We believe in giving back to our community, and our employees take pride in working at William Peace University. Department: Culture, History, and Politics Purpose of Department: The History, Culture, and Politics Department offers majors in: • Anthropology (BA) • Criminal Justice (BS and BA) • History and American Studies (BA) • Political Science (BA) • Pre-Law (BA) • Global Studies (BA) The department also offers minors in Anthropology, Criminal Justice, Forensics, History and American Studies, Political Science, and Global Studies. Anthropology Program Mission Statement: In taking as its broad scope the totality of human qualities and experience, the anthropology major at William Peace University seeks to promote in students a better understanding of and appreciation for human diversity, to develop a global awareness and conscience, and, as a result of its inherently interdisciplinary nature, to help students integrate their knowledge in the natural and social sciences, and the humanities. Anthropology’s emphasis on experiential, field-based learning will provide rich opportunities for student engagement, discovery, and adventure, and, thus, not only challenge students to become lifelong learners and pursue meaningful careers, but also to lead and serve others. Criminal Justice, Political Science, and Pre-Law Program Misson Statement: Challenging students to an adventure of intellectual understanding in the areas of criminal justice and the law for the purpose of developing responsible leaders and ethical citizens. This major aims to develop within students the critical and analytical skills to study criminal justice and the law and to be able to articulate information regarding criminal justice and law. Global Studies Program Misson Statement: The Global Studies Program engages students in the interdisciplinary study of the world so that they can find meaningful careers in a global environment, and can become more ethical global citizens and leaders. Summary of Position: William Peace University is continuously seeking qualified scholars for adjunct faculty positions in the Department of Culture, History & Politics who have demonstrated commitment to the promotion of interdisciplinary work, teaching excellence, diversity, and possess a collaborative leadership style. The successful candidates should have knowledge of and experience in their selected teaching discipline, as well as experience with and the ability to use instructional technologies to support classroom activities. Academic areas would include: • Anthropology • Criminal Justice • History and American Studies • Political Science • Global Studies Applications are accepted on a rolling basis and are reviewed as vacancies arise within the department. Essential duties and responsibilities: Teaching assignments would include lecture and laboratory instruction in courses for the Department of Culture, History & Politics.  Assignments may include classroom courses, online distance-education courses, or both. Depending on the department’s needs, selected candidates will be offered contracts to teach one or more course-sections for semester. Minimum Qualifications: •\tA Master’s degree in the teaching discipline, or a Master’s degree with a concentration in the teaching discipline (minimum of 18 graduate semester hours in discipline) •\tA demonstrated commitment to undergraduate teaching •\tRelated work experiences in the field, professional licensure and certifications, honors and awards, continuous documented excellence in teaching, or other demonstrated competencies and achievements that contribute to effective teaching and student learning outcomes may be used to supplement academic credentials if warranted •\tEstablished record of teaching excellence and demonstrated leadership experience. •\tA minimum of two years of work experience required Preferred Qualifications: •\tPh.D. in the teaching discipline •\t1-2 years teaching experience at the undergraduate level Hours per week: Varies by course load Job Posting Date: 01/30/2020 Priority Deadline: 12/18/2020 Priority Deadline Information: Priority consideration will be given to applications received by the Priority Date; however, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Please list the disciplines that you are interested in and qualified to teach at WPU.  Discipline options would include: Anthropology, Criminal Justice, History and American Studies, Political Science, Pre-Law and\r\nGlobal Studies. (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts Optional Documents Teaching Evaluations William Peace University 15 East Peace Street Raleigh, NC 27604 919.508.2000 Back to top Copyright © William Peace University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://peace.peopleadmin.com/postings/3104": {
      "title": "William Peace University Portal | Adjunct Instructor, Business - Fall 2026",
      "description": "William Peace University Portal | Adjunct Instructor, Business - Fall 2026 Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Careers Log In /Create Account Help Benefits of Working at WPU Adjunct Instructor, Business - Fall 2026 Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Positing Details Position Information Position Title: Adjunct Instructor, Business - Fall 2026 Posting Number: WPU0064217 University Information: William Peace University (“Peace”) provides a culture that fosters an energized team environment, builds on our strengths, promotes creativity and innovation, and encourages respect and open communication. We value our faculty and staff. We know they are important and vital to the growth of our university and culture. Senior leadership is personally dedicated to the professional growth and development of each employee. We want to help you build your career, while ensuring you have great work-life balance and flexibility. We teach our students the skills needed for ethical citizenship, not just in the classroom, but by example. We believe in giving back to our community, and our employees take pride in working at Peace. Department: Business Purpose of Department: The Department of Business is dedicated to providing a quality education in order to prepare students for their chosen careers or post-graduate studies. Summary of Position: William Peace University seeks qualified candidates to teach one or more of the following courses in the Business discipline for the Fall 2026 semester: BSA -160-02: Business in Our Global Society (TuTh 9:55-11:40 am) MGT -320-01: Project Management (MW 9:25-10:20 am) Instruction will take in-person, on-campus. Please use the supplemental questions included in the application to indicate which of the two courses you are interested in, qualified for, and are available to teach. This appointment will be from August 19, 2026 to December 14, 2026. Essential duties and responsibilities: BSA 160: Business in Our Global Society 4 credit hours Course Schedule: TuTh 9:55-11:40 am This course introduces business concepts and analyze how business influences our culture and society. Students will study and learn about business policies and practices from around the world. The course will explore the current international business environment including culture, infrastructure, investment, politics, trade, and economic development. Students will examine the strategies and structures of businesses operating in the global business environment. MGT 320: Project Management 2 credit hours Course Schedule: MW 9:25-10:20 am This course introduces key concepts in project management and the project management life cycle and provides an overview of industry leading project tracking applications. Upon completion, students should be able to effectively understand the 5 distinct phases of project management from planning to completion as well as how to lead through positive influence. The course will combine pedagogical concepts with practical examples. Minimum Qualifications: A Master’s degree in Business or closely related field Preferred Qualifications: A Doctoral degree in Business or closely related field Hours per week: Varies by course load Job Posting Date: 07/30/2026 Priority Deadline: 08/09/2026 Priority Deadline Information: Priority consideration will be given to applications received by the Priority Date; however, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Please list the courses that you are interest in and available to teach (mark all that apply) BSA-160-02: Business in Our Global Society TuTh 9:55-11:40 am (4 credits) MGT-320-01: Project Management MW 9:25-10:20 am (2 credits) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Teaching Evaluations William Peace University 15 East Peace Street Raleigh, NC 27604 919.508.2000 Back to top Copyright © William Peace University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
