    "https://peace.peopleadmin.com/postings/3110": {
      "title": "William Peace University Portal",
      "description": "William Peace University Portal | Public Safety Shift Supervisor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Careers Log In /Create Account Help Benefits of Working at WPU Public Safety Shift Supervisor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Positing Details Position Information Position Title: Public Safety Shift Supervisor Posting Number: WPU0061217 University Information: William Peace University (“Peace”) provides a culture that fosters an energized team environment, builds on our strengths, promotes creativity and innovation, and encourages respect and open communication. We value our faculty and staff. We know they are important and vital to the growth of our university and culture. Senior leadership is personally dedicated to the professional growth and development of each employee. We want to help you build your career, while ensuring you have great work-life balance and flexibility. We teach our students the skills needed for ethical citizenship, not just in the classroom, but by example. We believe in giving back to our community, and our employees take pride in working at Peace. Department: Public Safety Purpose of Department: The Office of Public Safety at William Peace University mission is to create and maintain a climate of security at William Peace University. A safe climate is necessary to enable the university to attract top students from around the world. It is also important to provide a safe and secure work and study environment that is free from concerns about crime and is conducive to the pursuit of a quality education. The public safety programs that are now in place were designed and implemented with this philosophy in mind. Summary of Position: The Public Safety Shift Supervisor oversees daily shift operations within the Department of Public Safety, ensuring a safe and secure campus environment for students, faculty, staff, and visitors. This role provides frontline leadership, supervises Public Safety Officers, and ensures the consistent application of policies, procedures, and emergency response protocols. Essential duties and responsibilities: Reporting to the Director of Public Safety, the individual holding this position is responsible for, but not limited to, the following duties: Serves as the lead officer and primary point of contact for the assigned shift, directing officers and delegating tasks Conduct roll call briefings, assign posts, and communicate priorities Monitor officer activity for productivity, professionalism, and compliance Provide real-time coaching, guidance, and corrective direction as needed Ensure proper staffing levels and adjust assignments based on campus needs Oversee patrol operations (foot, vehicle, and fixed posts) Ensure visibility and proactive engagement across campus Monitor access control, alarms, cameras, and emergency systems Respond to and oversee all major incidents and calls for service Act as the on-scene supervisor for critical incidents Coordinate response efforts until relieved by senior leadership or external agencies. Know when to appropriately escalate. Ensure proper documentation and reporting of all incidents Serve as liaison with local law enforcement, fire, and EMS when necessary Mentor and develop Public Safety Officers Assist with onboarding and field training of new hires Reinforce department standards, procedures, and customer service expectations Identify performance gaps and recommend additional training Review and approve incident reports for accuracy and completeness Prepare shift summaries and communicate key updates to leadership Track and report safety trends, concerns, and operational issues Promote a service-oriented approach to campus safety Ensure positive, professional interactions with campus community members De-escalate conflicts and support a welcoming campus environment Enforce university policies, regulations, and applicable laws Ensure adherence to Clery Act reporting requirements and campus safety standards Maintain accountability for officer conduct and departmental expectations Perform other Public Safety job-related duties and projects assigned. Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent 3–5 years of experience in campus safety, security, or law enforcement Demonstrated leadership or supervisory experience preferred Strong knowledge of emergency response procedures and incident management Excellent communication, report writing, and interpersonal skills Ability to make sound decisions under pressure Must possess a valid North Carolina driver’s license and good driving record. Preferred Qualifications: Experience in higher education/public safety environment Prior supervisory or lead officer experience Familiarity with Clery Act and campus safety compliance standards Certifications in CPR / AED , First Aid, or emergency management (e.g., ICS / NIMS ) Hours per week: 40 hrs. per week | 3rd Shift: Sunday to Thursday, 11:00 PM - 7:00 AM Job Posting Date: 08/12/2026 Priority Deadline: 08/26/2026 Priority Deadline Information: Priority consideration will be given to applications received by the Priority Date; however, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents William Peace University 15 East Peace Street Raleigh, NC 27604 919.508.2000 Back to top Copyright © William Peace University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://peace.peopleadmin.com/postings/2812": {
      "title": "William Peace University Portal",
      "description": "William Peace University Portal | Temporary/As Needed Public Safety Officer (Continuous Recruitment) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Careers Log In /Create Account Help Benefits of Working at WPU Temporary/As Needed Public Safety Officer (Continuous Recruitment) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Positing Details Position Information Position Title: Temporary/As Needed Public Safety Officer (Continuous Recruitment) Posting Number: WPU0026517 University Information: WPU provides a culture that fosters an energized team environment, builds on our strengths, promotes creativity and innovation, and encourages respect and open communication. We value our faculty and staff. We know they are important and vital to the growth of our university and culture. Senior leadership is personally dedicated to the professional growth and development of each employee. We want to help you build your career, while ensuring you have great work-life balance and flexibility. We teach our students the skills needed for ethical citizenship, not just in the classroom, but by example. We believe in giving back to our community, and our employees take pride in working at William Peace University. Department: Public Safety Purpose of Department: The Office of Public Safety’s mission is to create and maintain a climate of security at William Peace University. A safe climate is necessary to enable the university to attract top students from around the world. It is also important to provide a safe and secure work and study environment that is free from concerns about crime and is conducive to the pursuit of a quality education. The public safety programs that are now in place were designed and implemented with this philosophy in mind. Summary of Position: WPU seeks applicants to be available for duty as needed to cover planned and unplanned absences, emergency situations, and periods when additional staffing is required. Selected candidates will be contacted on an as needed basis throughout the year for various shifts. This position reports directly to the Director and the Assistant Director of Public Safety and provides general public safety services to the University community. This position is non-exempt (paid hourly) and the selected candidates must be able to satisfactorily clear a background check. Any hours worked on 2nd or 3rd shift will earn an additional 10% shift differential on top of base pay. Essential duties and responsibilities: Duties include but are not limited to enforcement of the University’s rules and policies; preventing and suppressing crime; protecting life and property; patrolling assigned areas on foot to ensure personnel, building, and equipment is secure; maintaining patrol logs, recording occurrences, and completing necessary paperwork; informing and warning violators of rule infractions such as loitering, smoking, or carrying forbidden articles; and working with local law enforcement agencies. Duties also may require use of computers to input and retrieve data. The Officer is expected to comply with the University’s and the Department’s rules, regulations, and policies; perform duties independently, utilize proper judgment, and maintain a high degree of professionalism. Minimum Qualifications: • High school diploma or equivalent • Minimum three years of experience in public safety • Possession of a valid North Carolina driver’s license • Previous experience working with diverse populations • Ability to maintain professionalism Preferred Qualifications: • Experience as a Police Officer • Experience in a public safety position in a higher education setting Hours per week: up to 29 based on dept needs Job Posting Date: 03/17/2021 Priority Deadline: 12/31/2021 Priority Deadline Information: Priority consideration will be given to applications received by the Priority Date; however, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). What hours and days of the week are you available for filling shifts in the Public Safety Office? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Resume William Peace University 15 East Peace Street Raleigh, NC 27604 919.508.2000 Back to top Copyright © William Peace University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://peace.peopleadmin.com/postings/3114": {
      "title": "William Peace University Portal | Assistant Coach, Men’s Volleyball (Part-Time)",
      "description": "William Peace University Portal | Assistant Coach, Men’s Volleyball (Part-Time) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Careers Log In /Create Account Help Benefits of Working at WPU Assistant Coach, Men’s Volleyball (Part-Time) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Positing Details Position Information Position Title: Assistant Coach, Men’s Volleyball (Part-Time) Posting Number: WPU0064617 University Information: William Peace University (“Peace”) provides a culture that fosters an energized team environment, builds on our strengths, promotes creativity and innovation, and encourages respect and open communication. We value our faculty and staff. We know they are important and vital to the growth of our university and culture. Senior leadership is personally dedicated to the professional growth and development of each employee. We want to help you build your career, while ensuring you have great work-life balance and flexibility. We teach our students the skills needed for ethical citizenship, not just in the classroom, but by example. We believe in giving back to our community, and our employees take pride in working at Peace. Department: Athletics Purpose of Department: The Athletic Department at William Peace University complements the institution’s core educational mission, helping to enrich the lives of our students while contributing to a vibrant and diverse campus community that inspires excellence. Our work contributes to the holistic educational environment and strengthens community at the University. Academic and athletic excellences are compatible in a well-balanced environment that encourages student-athletes to thrive and achieve their full potential as whole people. Summary of Position: Responsible for assisting the Head Coach in all aspects of planning, managing and developing a successful intercollegiate sports program in accordance with standards and goals set by William Peace University. This is a temporary part-time position with the general schedule including traditional and non-traditional seasons. Recruiting efforts will be determined by Head Coach with approval by the Director of Athletics. Essential duties and responsibilities: • Assist with practice plans, have knowledge of athletic conditioning and team physical training. • Must become proficient with Front Rush recruiting software • Must know and adhere to all NCAA and University regulations that relate to daily program management and operation of designated sport. • Assist with team and individual performance as well as develop and implement strategies for motivating student-athletes to perform at maximum levels as both individuals and a team. • Assist with the selection, purchase, fitting and maintenance of team equipment including uniforms and supplies. • Ensure the safety of student-athletes and staff through careful monitoring of the condition of equipment and facilities utilized by designated sport. • Assist with preparing game plans based on scouting reports and team evaluation. • Assist with game management of home athletic events, as requested. • Attend Athletic Department staff meetings, as requested. • Assist with approved fundraising activities, as requested. • Participate in clinics, exhibitions and camps, as approved. • Assist with recruiting as requested by the Head Coach and with approval of the Director of Athletics. Must know and adhere to all applicable NCAA and University regulations that relate to recruiting. • Effectively work with a diverse population of students, employees, visitors, and guests. • Other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: • Bachelor’s Degree • Coaching experience at the high school or collegiate level and/or playing experience at the collegiate level • Valid Driver’s License Preferred Qualifications: N/A Hours per week: 10 per week Job Posting Date: 08/27/2026 Priority Deadline: 09/04/2026 Priority Deadline Information: Priority consideration will be given to applications received by the Priority Date; however, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation William Peace University 15 East Peace Street Raleigh, NC 27604 919.508.2000 Back to top Copyright © William Peace University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://peace.peopleadmin.com/postings/2895": {
      "title": "William Peace University Portal | Adjunct Instructor, School of Professional Studies (Continuous Recruitment)",
      "description": "William Peace University Portal | Adjunct Instructor, School of Professional Studies (Continuous Recruitment) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Careers Log In /Create Account Help Benefits of Working at WPU Adjunct Instructor, School of Professional Studies (Continuous Recruitment) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Positing Details Position Information Position Title: Adjunct Instructor, School of Professional Studies (Continuous Recruitment) Posting Number: WPU0003317 University Information: WPU provides a culture that fosters an energized team environment, builds on our strengths, promotes creativity and innovation, and encourages respect and open communication. We value our faculty and staff. We know they are important and vital to the growth of our university and culture. Senior leadership is personally dedicated to the professional growth and development of each employee. We want to help you build your career, while ensuring you have great work-life balance and flexibility. We teach our students the skills needed for ethical citizenship, not just in the classroom, but by example. We believe in giving back to our community, and our employees take pride in working at William Peace University. Department: School of Professional Studies Purpose of Department: The School of Professional Studies provides online and classroom-based programs of study that are responsive of students’ needs preparing them for lifelong learning, meaningful careers, and ethical citizenship through intellectual opportunities in a student-focused environment. Summary of Position: William Peace University is continuously seeking qualified scholars for adjunct faculty positions in the School of Professional Studies who have demonstrated commitment to the promotion of interdisciplinary work, teaching excellence, diversity, and possess a collaborative leadership style. The successful candidates should have knowledge of and experience in their selected teaching discipline, as well as experience with and the ability to use instructional technologies to support classroom activities. Academic areas would include: • Accounting • Communications • Finance • Leadership • Management Applications are accepted on a rolling basis and are reviewed as vacancies arise within the department. Essential duties and responsibilities: Teaching assignments would include lecture and laboratory instruction in courses for the School of Professional Studies may include classroom courses, online distance-education courses, or both. Depending on the department’s needs, selected candidates will be offered contracts to teach one or more course-sections for semester. Minimum Qualifications: • A Master’s degree in the teaching discipline, or a Master’s degree with a concentration in the teaching discipline (minimum of 18 graduate semester hours in discipline) • A demonstrated commitment to undergraduate teaching • Related work experiences in the field, professional licensure and certifications, honors and awards, continuous documented excellence in teaching, or other demonstrated competencies and achievements that contribute to effective teaching and student learning outcomes may be used to supplement academic credentials if warranted • Established record of teaching excellence and demonstrated leadership experience. • A minimum of two years of work experience required Preferred Qualifications: • Ph.D. in the teaching discipline • 1-2 years teaching experience at the undergraduate level Hours per week: Varies by course load Job Posting Date: 01/29/2020 Priority Deadline: 12/18/2020 Priority Deadline Information: Priority consideration will be given to applications received by the Priority Date; however, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please list the disciplines that you are interested in and qualified to teach at WPU.  Discipline options would include: Accounting, Communications, Finance, Leadership\r\nand Management. (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Teaching Evaluations William Peace University 15 East Peace Street Raleigh, NC 27604 919.508.2000 Back to top Copyright © William Peace University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
