    "https://peace.peopleadmin.com/postings/3065": {
      "title": "William Peace University Portal | Maintenance Technician",
      "description": "William Peace University Portal | Maintenance Technician Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Careers Log In /Create Account Help Benefits of Working at WPU Maintenance Technician Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Positing Details Position Information Position Title: Maintenance Technician Posting Number: WPU0061517 University Information: William Peace University (“Peace”) provides a culture that fosters an energized team environment, builds on our strengths, promotes creativity and innovation, and encourages respect and open communication. We value our faculty and staff. We know they are important and vital to the growth of our university and culture. Senior leadership is personally dedicated to the professional growth and development of each employee. We want to help you build your career, while ensuring you have great work-life balance and flexibility. We teach our students the skills needed for ethical citizenship, not just in the classroom, but by example. We believe in giving back to our community, and our employees take pride in working at Peace. Department: Buildings and Grounds Purpose of Department: The mission of the department of Building and Grounds at William Peace University is to create and support a well-maintained campus infrastructure and to provide the highest quality service in a responsive and efficient manner to all our students, staff, faculty and visitors. Summary of Position: The Maintenance Technician performs preventative maintenance and journeyman-level repair of William Peace University facilities from multiple trade areas including: electrical, plumbing, HVAC , drywall, painting, and carpentry. The Maintenance Technician also performs basic vehicle maintenance and grounds-keeping work as needed to ensure that university vehicles and grounds are maintained appropriately. Reporting to the Associate Vice President ( AVP ) for Facilities, the Maintenance Technician functions independently performing tasks received through an online work order system and from direction given by the AVP . The Maintenance Technician collaborates with the AVP , vendors, and contractors as required on complex and unusual maintenance requests and problems. Essential duties and responsibilities: Reporting to the Associate Vice President for Buildings & Grounds, the individual holding this position is responsible for, but not limited to, the following duties: Respond to work order requests in professional and timely manner documenting work activities and resolutions to issues. Determine appropriate repairs and solutions based on the details provided in the work order and through communication with the reporting party, supervisor, etc. Identify the cause of a problem, determine materials, tools needed, and methods of best corrective action needed to prevent recurrence. The technician is expected to carry repair procedures independently. Participate in project planning and completion of discussions. Install, maintain, alter, or repair plumbing, HVAC , and electrical fixtures. Carpentry requirements include the ability to understand design tools (drawings), use of tools/equipment and complete as designed for the project. Repair/replace small motors and pumps. Install /relace electrical fixtures and components. Prep walls and surfaces for interior and exterior painting. Paint surfaces using brushes, rollers and spray methods. Install and change out fixtures; clear lines, run lines as related to plumbing issues. Perform basic maintenance on vehicles, golf carts and yard equipment. Maintain maintenance schedule and ensure that preventative maintenance is performed by outside vendors in timely fashion. Assist grounds technicians when needed. This may include seeding; mowing; installing plants; trimming; edging; performing general care of grass and flower beds; maintaining paths, roads, and parking lots; and participating in the removal of dirt, rubbish, snow, leaves, and refuse. Use hand and power tools to complete assigned tasks. This position is considered mandatory/essential and will be required on campus under all conditions of the Adverse Weather and Emergency Closing policies. Perform other job-related duties and projects assigned. PHYSICAL DEMANDS The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. The employee is occasionally required to climb or balance and stoop, kneel, crouch, or crawl. Specific vision abilities required by this job include close vision, peripheral vision, depth perception, and ability to adjust focus. Frequently is required to walk, sit, stand, and reach with hands and arms; and talk or hear. Must frequently lift and carry up to 25 pounds regularly and up to 50 pounds occasionally. Exhibit manual dexterity to operate both office and building maintenance related equipment. WORK ENVIRONMENT The work environment characteristics described here are representative of those an employee encounters while performing the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Work is frequently performed outdoors with occasional exposure to adverse climate and weather conditions such as wind, sun, and hot or cold temperatures and with noise levels varying from moderate to loud. Work is also performed indoors with varying temperatures and with noise levels varying from moderate to loud. While performing the duties of this job, the employee is frequently exposed to moving mechanical parts and outside weather conditions. The employee is occasionally exposed to high, precarious places; fumes or airborne particles; toxic or caustic chemicals; risk of electrical shock; and vibration. Minimum Qualifications: High school graduation or GED with at least two years of relevant experience in trades. Certifications if/as required by any assigned tasks. Must possess working knowledge of the methods, practices, and materials used in the effective maintenance and repair of commercial and residential buildings. Must be able to operate equipment including: yard equipment, manlifts, vehicles. Must be able to work in tight spaces and various heights using ladders and lifts. Must be able to follow oral and written instructions. Must be able to read diagrams and MSDS and produce written documentation of work assignments. Must be available for emergency call-back during the evening and on weekends. Occasional overtime. Must be able to lift 50 pounds. Must possess a valid NC driver’s license or have the ability to obtain one within 60 days of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Five or more years of relevant, progressive experience in trades. Experience reading blueprints, schematics, and drawings. Experience using an automated work order system. Experience using Microsoft Office Suite. Hours per week: 40 hours Job Posting Date: 06/15/2026 Priority Deadline: 06/30/2026 Priority Deadline Information: Priority consideration will be given to applications received by the Priority Date; however, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter William Peace University 15 East Peace Street Raleigh, NC 27604 919.508.2000 Back to top Copyright © William Peace University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://peace.peopleadmin.com/postings/3076": {
      "title": "William Peace University Portal | Instructor, Exercise and Sport Science (Fall 2026)",
      "description": "William Peace University Portal | Instructor, Exercise and Sport Science (Fall 2026) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Careers Log In /Create Account Help Benefits of Working at WPU Instructor, Exercise and Sport Science (Fall 2026) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Positing Details Position Information Position Title: Instructor, Exercise and Sport Science (Fall 2026) Posting Number: WPU0063217 University Information: William Peace University (“Peace”) provides a culture that fosters an energized team environment, builds on our strengths, promotes creativity and innovation, and encourages respect and open communication. We value our faculty and staff. We know they are important and vital to the growth of our university and culture. Senior leadership is personally dedicated to the professional growth and development of each employee. We want to help you build your career, while ensuring you have great work-life balance and flexibility. We teach our students the skills needed for ethical citizenship, not just in the classroom, but by example. We believe in giving back to our community, and our employees take pride in working at Peace. Department: Exercise and Sport Science Purpose of Department: The Department of Exercise and Sports Science is dedicated to providing a quality education in order to prepare students for their chosen careers or post-graduate studies. Summary of Position: William Peace University seeks qualified candidates to teach one or more of the following courses in the Exercise & Sport Science discipline for the Fall 2026 semester: ESS 300: Kinesiology ( MWF 8:00-9:15 am) PEH 154: Pilates (TTh 9:55-10:50 am) course begins October 14 Instruction will take in-person, on-campus. Please use the supplemental questions included in the application to indicate which of the two (or both) courses you are interested in, qualified for, and are available to teach. This appointment will be from August 19, 2026 to December 10, 2026. Essential duties and responsibilities: ESS 300: Kinesiology 4 credit hours Prerequisite: ESS 110 Course Schedule: MWF 8-9:15 a.m. The study of musculoskeletal anatomy, physiology, and mechanics in relation to human movement. Special emphasis will be placed on the study of bones, joints, muscles, and their relation to sport and exercise. PEH 154: Pilates 1 credit hour Course Schedule: TTh 9:55-10:50 a.m. (begins October 14) This course is a introduction to the fundamentals and exercises of Pilates mat work. Based on the work of Joseph H. Pilates, students learn this integrated system of movement, breath, and experiential anatomical awareness to increase core body strength, flexibility, and range of motion. Minimum Qualifications: • A Master’s degree in Kinesiology, Exercise Physiology or closely related field (including but not limited to Exercise and Sport Science, Exercise Physiology, Physiology, or Rehabilitation Sciences) Preferred Qualifications: • A Doctoral degree in Kinesiology or closely related field (including but not limited to Exercise and Sport Science, Exercise Physiology, Physiology, or Rehabilitation Sciences) • Certification with ACSM , NSCA , or NASM Hours per week: Varies by course load Job Posting Date: 07/09/2026 Priority Deadline: 07/30/2026 Priority Deadline Information: Priority consideration will be given to applications received by the Priority Date; however, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Please list the courses that you are interest in and available to teach (mark all that apply) ESS 300: Kinesiology MWF 8-9:15 a.m. (4 credits) PEH 154: Pilates TTh 9:55-10:50 a.m. (begins October 14) (1 credit) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Teaching Evaluations William Peace University 15 East Peace Street Raleigh, NC 27604 919.508.2000 Back to top Copyright © William Peace University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://peace.peopleadmin.com/postings/3097": {
      "title": "William Peace University Portal | Adjunct Instructor, Department of Business (Continuous Recruitment)",
      "description": "William Peace University Portal | Adjunct Instructor, Department of Business (Continuous Recruitment) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Careers Log In /Create Account Help Benefits of Working at WPU Adjunct Instructor, Department of Business (Continuous Recruitment) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Positing Details Position Information Position Title: Adjunct Instructor, Department of Business (Continuous Recruitment) Posting Number: WPU0002917 University Information: WPU provides a culture that fosters an energized team environment, builds on our strengths, promotes creativity and innovation, and encourages respect and open communication. We value our faculty and staff. We know they are important and vital to the growth of our university and culture. Senior leadership is personally dedicated to the professional growth and development of each employee. We want to help you build your career, while ensuring you have great work-life balance and flexibility. We teach our students the skills needed for ethical citizenship, not just in the classroom, but by example. We believe in giving back to our community, and our employees take pride in working at William Peace University. Department: Psychology and Business Purpose of Department: The mission of the Business Administration Program at William Peace University supports the Mission and the Strategic Plan of the College. Therefore, the mission of the Business Administration Program is to provide exceptional, innovative, and social-responsibility based programs. The programs prepare students with the core competencies and skills necessary to manage and lead the workforce, and with the fundamental knowledge required for the pursuit of graduate studies in a highly turbulent global environment. The commitment of our dedicated faculty, staff, and administrators is to enhance the knowledge base and to encourage life-long learning that empowers students in the Business Administration Program, and is consistent with the traditions of excellence, integrity, liberal arts education, and community. Summary of Position: William Peace University is continuously seeking qualified scholars for adjunct faculty positions in the Department of Business. Ideal candidates will be those who have demonstrated commitment to the promotion of interdisciplinary work, teaching excellence, diversity, and possess a collaborative leadership style. The successful candidates should have knowledge of and experience in their selected teaching discipline, as well as experience with and the ability to use instructional technologies to support classroom activities. Applications are accepted on a rolling basis and are reviewed as vacancies arise within the department. Essential duties and responsibilities: Teaching assignments would include lecture instruction in courses at the introductory level as well as marketing electives for the Department of Business. This position will be responsible for the Advertising and Marketing Research courses. Assignments may include classroom courses, online distance-education courses, or both. Depending on the department’s needs, selected candidates will be offered contracts to teach one or more course-sections for semester. Minimum Qualifications: • A Master’s degree in the teaching discipline, or a Master’s degree with a concentration in the teaching discipline (minimum of 18 graduate semester hours in discipline) • A demonstrated commitment to undergraduate teaching • Related work experiences in the field, professional licensure and certifications, honors and awards, continuous documented excellence in teaching, or other demonstrated competencies and achievements that contribute to effective teaching and student learning outcomes may be used to supplement academic credentials if warranted • Established record of teaching excellence and demonstrated leadership experience. • A minimum of two years of work experience required Preferred Qualifications: • Ph.D. in the teaching discipline • 1-2 years teaching experience at the undergraduate level Hours per week: Varies by course load Job Posting Date: 01/30/2020 Priority Deadline: 12/18/2020 Priority Deadline Information: Priority consideration will be given to applications received by the Priority Date; however, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Please list the disciplines that you are interested in and qualified to teach at WPU. (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts Optional Documents Teaching Evaluations William Peace University 15 East Peace Street Raleigh, NC 27604 919.508.2000 Back to top Copyright © William Peace University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://peace.peopleadmin.com/postings/3099": {
      "title": "William Peace University Portal | Director of Student Involvement",
      "description": "William Peace University Portal | Director of Student Involvement Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Careers Log In /Create Account Help Benefits of Working at WPU Director of Student Involvement Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Positing Details Position Information Position Title: Director of Student Involvement Posting Number: WPU0064017 University Information: William Peace University (“Peace”) provides a culture that fosters an energized team environment, builds on our strengths, promotes creativity and innovation, and encourages respect and open communication. We value our faculty and staff. We know they are important and vital to the growth of our university and culture. Senior leadership is personally dedicated to the professional growth and development of each employee. We want to help you build your career, while ensuring you have great work-life balance and flexibility. We teach our students the skills needed for ethical citizenship, not just in the classroom, but by example. We believe in giving back to our community, and our employees take pride in working at Peace. Department: Student Involvement Purpose of Department: The Office of Student Life at William Peace University strives to enhance the Pacer experience through the development of the whole student from deposit until graduation. Summary of Position: The Director of Student Involvement is responsible for identifying, developing and training student leaders; developing, organizing, and facilitating a university-wide leadership program; advising the Student Government and Programming Association; organizing and managing a process to assess student programs and events; advising students and registering student organizations in event planning and management; supervising and training full time, graduate, and student staff members as assigned; and assisting in the development and implementation of student life programs, policies and procedures. May share in an on-call rotation; responding to student crisis situations after hours. Essential duties and responsibilities: Reporting to the Assistant Vice President for Student Life, the individual holding this position is responsible for, but not limited to, the following duties: Orientation and Family Services Oversee the planning, execution, and assessment of the University Onboarding programs including New Student, Transfer, and Parent/Family Orientation Recruit, hire, train, and supervise Orientation Leaders Provide strategic oversight and direction for Family Services, including family engagement initiatives, family communications, and events that support student success, in collaboration with campus partners. Student Government and Programming Association and Registered Student Organizations Serve as the executive-level advisor to the Student Government and Programming Association ( SGPA ) executive council including conducting regular one-on-one meetings with the President and Vice President. Manage the election process for Student Government Programming Association Collaborate with SGPA on the allocation and regulation of the Student Activity Fee account to support campus-wide programs related to student organizations or campus departments Oversee all conduct related to RSOs, including the creation and enforcement of campus policies, internal and external behaviors and risk management Oversee and assess all training related to student organizations Assist in the development and implementation of campus programming and events sponsored by SGPA Advise and/or plan all major campus-wide traditions including but not limited to Fall Cocktail, Red Rose Ball, Traditions Dinner, WPU Holiday Celebration and Last Day of Classes Festival ( LDOC ), including event logistics, budget and vendor management and assessment Collaborate with SGPA to oversee Student Life Facilities including the SGPA office space and the game room Plan and execute annual student and alumni programming, travel opportunities, and commencement events Leadership Development Develop and implement strategic goals and programs to enhance the leadership development of the Traditional Undergraduate population Create and oversee the implementation of leadership development programming including trainings, overnight retreats, workshops Foster collaborative relationships with Academic Affairs and other Student Life partners to strengthen leadership programming Civic Engagement and Community Service Provide oversight to the Program Coordinator of Student Life to create a robust and comprehensive civic engagement program Assist in the planning and implementation of the annual MLK Day of Service, Alternative Fall Break and Alternative Spring Break programs Ensure compliance with federal mandates related to community service and reporting of service hours Office Oversight and General Duties Oversee department assessment Oversee various Student Activity budgets Create marketing and communication for students regarding student involvement activities Manage Student Life social media Serve on various University committees Evaluate and assess office’s programming, policies and procedures on a regular basis including the completion of the institution’s annual institutional effectiveness process Serve as the primary contract negotiator and executor for the office and its recognized organizations, in compliance with university policy and fiscal procedure Cultivate meaningful partnerships and collaborative opportunities with constituents on and off-campus Oversee the office’s representation at various campus events, admissions programs and presentations to classes including Peace Preview and Admitted Students Day Perform other job-related duties and projects assigned. SUPERVISORY RESPONSIBILITIES Directly supervise the Assistant Director of Student Life, Program Coordinator for Student Life, and the Student and Family Specialist. Indirectly supervise Graduate Assistants, Interns, and Orientation Leaders. Responsibilities include interviewing, hiring, and training employees; planning, assigning, and directing work; appraising performance; and rewarding and disciplining employees. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s Degree in higher education (or related field) with 5 years of experience in a higher education institution or Master’s Degree in higher education (or related field) with 3 years of experience in a higher education institution. Preferred Qualifications: Experience at a small private institution, experience advising student organization, experience working with student government associations, supervision experience. Hours per week: 40 Job Posting Date: 07/29/2026 Priority Deadline: 08/12/2026 Priority Deadline Information: Priority consideration will be given to applications received by the Priority Date; however, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation William Peace University 15 East Peace Street Raleigh, NC 27604 919.508.2000 Back to top Copyright © William Peace University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
