    "https://peace.peopleadmin.com/postings/3116": {
      "title": "William Peace University Portal | Assistant Coach, Women’s Lacrosse",
      "description": "William Peace University Portal | Assistant Coach, Women’s Lacrosse Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Careers Log In /Create Account Help Benefits of Working at WPU Assistant Coach, Women’s Lacrosse Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Positing Details Position Information Position Title: Assistant Coach, Women’s Lacrosse Posting Number: WPU0064717 University Information: William Peace University (“Peace”) provides a culture that fosters an energized team environment, builds on our strengths, promotes creativity and innovation, and encourages respect and open communication. We value our faculty and staff. We know they are important and vital to the growth of our university and culture. Senior leadership is personally dedicated to the professional growth and development of each employee. We want to help you build your career, while ensuring you have great work-life balance and flexibility. We teach our students the skills needed for ethical citizenship, not just in the classroom, but by example. We believe in giving back to our community, and our employees take pride in working at Peace. Department: Athletics Purpose of Department: The Athletic Department at William Peace University complements the institution’s core educational mission, helping to enrich the lives of our students while contributing to a vibrant and diverse campus community that inspires excellence. Our work contributes to the holistic educational environment and strengthens community at the University. Academic and athletic excellences are compatible in a well-balanced environment that encourages student-athletes to thrive and achieve their full potential as whole people. Summary of Position: The Assistant Coach, Women’s Lacrosse, is responsible for assisting with all aspects of planning, managing and developing a successful intercollegiate Women’s Lacrosse program in accordance with the standards and goals set by William Peace University. Essential duties and responsibilities: Adhere to all applicable NCAA and university regulations that relate to recruiting, daily program management and operation of the individual sport. Recruit quality student athletes by means of personal contact, phone and written correspondence with player, coach and parents. Evaluate ability either in person or through videotape analysis. Make frequent off-campus trips to watch games/matches/meets. Assist in arranging on-campus visits for prospective student athletes while ensuring compliance with NCAA guidelines for contacting and entertaining prospects. Assist in scheduling games, practices, facility and vehicle use in conjunction with the Head Coach and other WPU staff. Assist in scheduling and planning practices. Ensure compliance with NCAA regulations on Playing Season. Per NCAA Bylaw 17.01 and 17.02 Assist with approved fundraising activities, as requested. Assist with team travel in conjunction with the Head Coach. Evaluate team and individual performance. Develop and implement strategies for motivating student-athletes to perform at maximum levels as both individuals and a team. Effectively work with a diverse population of students, employees, visitors, and guests. Monitor the condition of playing equipment and facilities used by his/her team to ensure the safety of student-athletes and staff. Monitor the eligibility status and promote the academic progress of student-athletes. Responsible for campus facilities and equipment during practices/home sporting events. Possess a comprehensive knowledge of athletic conditioning and team physical training. Prepare game plans based on scouting reports and team evaluation. Participate in, organize, and lead clinics, exhibitions, and camps, as approved. Minimum Qualifications: • Bachelor’s degree • Valid driver’s license Preferred Qualifications: • Collegiate coaching experience • Certification in CPR , AED and First Aid Hours per week: 10 Job Posting Date: 08/27/2026 Priority Deadline: 09/04/2026 Priority Deadline Information: Priority consideration will be given to applications received by the Priority Date; however, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation William Peace University 15 East Peace Street Raleigh, NC 27604 919.508.2000 Back to top Copyright © William Peace University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
